<title>UK: CULVER TO SELL TRAVEL INSURANCE BUSINESSES.</title>
<headline>CULVER TO SELL TRAVEL INSURANCE BUSINESSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Culver Holdings Plc said on Wednesday that it is selling its travel insurance businesses to Financial Insurance Group Services Ltd, a unit of GE Capital Services, for up to 4.75 million stg in cash.</p>
<p>The sale includes the businesses of WorldCover Direct, Accident &amp; General, Bawden &amp; Co and Direct Insurance Prodcuts.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
